:1986-01-21-bell-296b-id-3072
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Bell 296B";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "04:25";
        ex:operator              "Air Taxi";
        ex:passengersAboard      "3"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "3"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Minnesota";
        dcterms:date             "1986-01-21"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The purpose of the flight was to take a news crew to a location to cover a story. The news crew had attempted to hire another helicopter, but that operator refused due to forecast low visibility. This pilot, however, agreed to fly. Although he was certified for instrument flight in airplanes, the pilot was not qualified for instrument flight in helicopters, nor was the helicopter certified for instrument flight. The helicopter crashed & burned approximately 100' from the highway near a power line crossing. Impact occurred while the helicopter was in a shallow descent, heading away from the highway & parallel with the power line. Continued VFR flight into IMC. Overconfidence in personal ability.";
        schema:location          "Ellendale" .

