:1951-12-16-curtiss-wright-c-46f-id-3313
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Curtiss Wright C-46F";
        ex:groundFatalities      "1"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "15:09";
        ex:operator              "Miami Airlines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "56"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "56"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "New Jersey";
        ex:route                 "Fort Smith - Newark";
        dcterms:date             "1951-12-16"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "Shortly after taking off from Newark Airport the control tower noticed smoke emanating from the right engine.  Minutes later the aircraft gradually descended, its left wing dropped and the aircraft struck the roof of a vacant building. Hold-down studs in the number 10 cylinder of the right engine failed due to fatigue. Fire erupted at the base of the failed cylinder. Extension of the landing gear and loss of the right engine led to the aircraft stalling at the height of about 200 ft. The aircraft was also overloaded by 117 pounds. A stall with the landing gear extended following a serious loss of power from the right engine. This loss of power was caused by the failure of the hold-down studs of the No. 10 cylinder, precipitating a fire in flight which became uncontrollable.";
        schema:location          "Elizabeth" .

:2009-02-12-bombardier-dhc-8-402-q400-id-3384
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Bombardier DHC-8-402 Q400";
        ex:groundFatalities      "1"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "22:17";
        ex:operator              "Continental Connection/Colgan Air";
        ex:passengersAboard      "49"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "49"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "New York";
        ex:route                 "Newark, N.J. - Buffalo, NY";
        dcterms:date             "2009-02-12"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The commuter plane crashed while attemptiong to land in rain and sleet, 6 miles northeast of Buffalo Niagara International Airport, were it was scheduled to land. Preliminary evidence suggests the crew selected the landing gear down and set the flaps 15 degrees. Immediately after selecting the flaps the stick shaker activated. The captain then pulled on the controls, slowing the airplane even further causing the plane to stall.";
        schema:location          "Clarence Center" .

:1940-12-04-douglas-dc-3a-id-2263
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Douglas DC-3A";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "17:48";
        ex:operator              "United Air Lines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "16"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "10"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Illinois";
        ex:route                 "New York City - Chicago";
        dcterms:date             "1940-12-04"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The aircraft crashed while attempting to land at Chicago. The failure of the pilot to exercise that degree of caution and skill required to avert a stall while approaching for a landing on the short northwest runway. A substantial contributing factor to the accident was the error in judgment of the pilot in choosing that short runway for his landing. An accumulation of ice on the wings may have increased the stalling speed of the plane.";
        schema:location          "Chicago" .

