        ex:region                "Italy";
        ex:route                 "Rome - Athens";
        dcterms:date             "1964-11-23"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The captain decided to abort the takeoff after the No. 4 engine pressure ratio read zero thrust and the amber warning light indicating thrust reversal of No. 2 engine came on. The speed was below V1. The aircraft continued to travel past the runway limit and the No. 4 engine struck a steam roller. The aircraft burst into flames. Malfunction of the No. 2 engine reverse thruster. The malfunction allowed in the development of forward thrust by No. 2 engine even though all four levers were in the reverse position.";
        schema:location          "Rome" .

