        dcterms:description      "The pilot of the cargo flight reported he had an asymmetrifuel condition. The pilot  asked for a lower altitude and controllers cleared the flight to 4,000 feet. About a minute later the pilot transmitted six 'Maydays.' The airplane then descended in  a near vertical dive until it crashed into a pasture. The pilot's inflight loss of control following a reported fuel asymmetry condition for undetermined reasons.";
        schema:location          "Near Paris" .

