        schema:location          "Rome" .

:1962-09-23-lockheed-1049h-82-super-constellation-id-5148
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Lockheed 1049H-82 Super Constellation";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "21:00";
        ex:operator              "Flying Tiger Line";
        ex:passengersAboard      "76"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "28"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "North AtlantiOcean";
        ex:route                 "Gander, Newfoundland - Frankfurt, Germany";
        dcterms:date             "1962-09-23"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "A fire developed in the No. 3 engine. A few minutes later, the propeller of the No. 1 engine oversped and the flight engineer inadvertently closed the firewall shutoff valve to the No. 1 engine. The No. 1 engine was then shut down. The No. 2 engine then developed mechanical trouble. The plane ditched at sea approximately 560 nm W of Shannon, Ireland. Failure of 2 of the 4 aircraft's engines and the improper action of the flight engineer which disabled a 3rd engine necessitating a ditching at sea." .

