        ex:route                 "Boston - NY - Washington DC - Jacksonville - Miami";
        dcterms:date             "1945-07-12"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "After deviating off course 8 miles to avoid military traffic, the two planes collided at 3,000 ft. The commercial pilot landed the plane in a corn field.  Two occupants of the A-26 (33-35553) were killed and one parachuted safely. One infant was killed on the DC-3.  Lack of vigilance on the part  of the pilots of both aircraft, resulting in the failure of each pilot to see the other aircraft in time to  avoid a collision.";
        schema:location          "Near Florence" .

