        schema:location          "Near Cebu" .

:1937-10-17-douglas-dc-3-id-4986
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Douglas DC-3";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "21:00";
        ex:operator              "United Air Lines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "19"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "19"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Wyoming";
        ex:route                 "Cheyenne - Salt Lake City";
        dcterms:date             "1937-10-17"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The plane crashed into the side of a mountain (Humpy Ridge)  in level flight at 10,000 ft. under adverse weather conditions. Staticonditions encountered in the last portion of the flight which rendered the reception of radio range signals unintelligible. The continuation of the flight into mountainous country at an altitude below of higher mountains without the aid of ground visibility or radio signals to definitely identify position. A change in the weather caused by the approach of an unpredicted cold front.";
        schema:location          "Haydens Peak" .

:1995-06-09-de-havilland-canada-dhc-8-102-id-3445
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "de Havilland Canada DHC-8-102";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "09:22";
        ex:operator              "Ansett New Zealand";
        ex:passengersAboard      "21"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "5"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "New Zealand";
        ex:route                 "Auckland - Palmerston North";
        dcterms:date             "1995-06-09"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "As the plane approached  Runway 25,  the right main landing gear did not extend. While the captain continued the descent the co-pilot carried out the landing gear alternate extension checklist. The plane descended below the minimum safe step-down altitudes for the approach and struck the top of a ridge line. The captain did not ensure the aircraft intercepted and maintained the approach profile during the non-precision instrument approach. The captain's  unwise decision to get the landing gear lowered without discontinuing the instrument approach. The captain's distraction from the primary task of flying the aircraft safely during the first officer's attempt  to correct a landing gear malfunction.";
        schema:location          "Near Palmerston North" .

