:1980-08-19-lockheed-1011-200-tristar-id-4171
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Lockheed 1011-200 TriStar";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "19:08";
        ex:operator              "Saudi Arabian Airlines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "301"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "301"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Saudi Arabia";
        ex:route                 "Riyadh - Jeddah";
        dcterms:date             "1980-08-19"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The flight experienced a fire in the aft cargo compartment  6 minutes after taking off from Rilyadh. The plane returned to the airport and landed but because of a delay in evacuating the plane, all aboard were killed by smoke and fire. Half a minute before landing the captain decided not to order an emergency evacuation.  When he landed, he did not stop immediately but instead proceeded to make a normal landing delaying the fire equipment from putting out the fire. It took a full twenty-three minutes after touchdown before the doors were opened. The failure of the captain to prepare the cabin crew for immediate evacuation upon landing and his failure in not making a maximum stop landing on the runway, with immediate evacuation.";
        schema:location          "Near Riyadh" .

