:1960-03-17-lockheed-188c-electra-id-2397
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Lockheed 188C Electra";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "15:25";
        ex:operator              "Northwest Orient Airlines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "63"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "63"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Indiana";
        ex:route                 "Chicago - Miami";
        dcterms:date             "1960-03-17"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "An in-flight separation of the wing. A design flaw caused an oscillation known as whirl mode to transfer propeller wobble to the outboard nacelles which induced flutter in the wing which led to the separation of the wing. Reduced stiffness of the structure and the entry of the aircraft into an area of severe clear air turbulence were contributing factors. One of two crashes with the same cause.  See 9/29/59.";
        schema:location          "10 mile SE of Tell City" .

:1962-10-19-convair-cv-340-440-id-1472
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Convair CV-340/440";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "20:52";
        ex:operator              "Allegheny Airlines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "52"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "1"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Connecticut";
        ex:route                 "Washington D.C. - Providence, RI";
        dcterms:date             "1962-10-19"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "Following departure from Philadelphia, a high frequency whistling noise was heard and inspection revealed an escape of air at the lower aft corner of the rear service door. Pillow cases were placed in this area to reduce the air noise but no further action was taken. While the aircraft was descending through 4,000 feet the door blew out. The ensuing outward rush of air ejected a flight attendant who was near the door opening. Undetected insecure latching of the rear service door, resulting in an inflight explosive decompression which ejected a flight attendant from the aircraft.";
        schema:location          "Windsor Locks" .

:1954-09-12-douglas-dc-3-id-724
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Douglas DC-3";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "20:08";
        ex:operator              "Cruzeiro";
        ex:passengersAboard      "30"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "6"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Brazil";
        dcterms:date             "1954-09-12"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The plane was attemping to return to the Rio de Janeiro after severe vibrations in the No. 1 engine made the crew feather the prop.  While on final the aircraft came in too high and a go-around was attempted during which the plane crashed into the sea.   Lack of reference to instruments after opening the throttle to go-around in restricted visibility.  Power may have been inadvertently reduced on the good engine.";
        schema:location          "Off Rio de Janeiro" .

