        ex:region                "New York";
        ex:route                 "Pan Am building - JFK Airport";
        dcterms:date             "1977-05-16"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "While passengers were loading aboard the helicopter on top of the Pan Am building, the landing  gear collapsed causing the helicopter to tip on its side.  Four people, waiting to board the craft  were killed by the rotating blades. One of the blades tore loose and struck a window breaking in two. One-half of the blade then sailed two blocks striking and killing a pedestrian. Fatigue failure of the upper right forward fitting of the right main landing gear tube assembly. The fatigue originated from a small surface pit of undetermined source.";
        schema:location          "New York" .

