        ex:hour                  "19:21";
        ex:operator              "Scandinavian Airlines (SAS)";
        ex:passengersAboard      "45"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "15"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "California";
        ex:route                 "Copenhagen - Los Angeles - Seattle";
        dcterms:date             "1969-01-13"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The aircraft was on approach to 07R when it crashed into Santa Monica Bay 6 miles short of the runway. The fuselage  broke into 3 pieces one of which floated for 20 hours. SAS did not authorize a back course approach to LAX.  A VOR approach was conducted without notifying the controlling authority. The crew was preoccupied with a landing gear light problem. Lack of crew coordination and inadequate monitoring of aircraft position which resulted in an unplanned descent into the water. The aircraft was named 'Sverre Viking.'";
        schema:location          "Off Los Angeles" .

