        ex:region                "Nigeria";
        ex:route                 "Port Harcourt - Lagos";
        dcterms:date             "1996-11-07"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The plane crashed mid-way along its scheduled 50 minute route. The aircraft went into a roll and lost control after taking evasive action to avoid another aircraft. The plane was flying almost at the speed of sound when it crashed and disintegrated. ATC error. The controller thought he had cleared to aircraft to FL100 but the aircraft was still flying at FL240.";
        schema:location          "Lagos" .

:1985-08-02-lockheed-l-1011-1-tristar-id-4534
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Lockheed L-1011-1 TriStar";
        ex:groundFatalities      "1"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "18:06";
        ex:operator              "Delta Air Lines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "163"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "134"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Texas";
        ex:route                 "Fort Lauderdale - Dallas-Fort Worth";
        dcterms:date             "1985-08-02"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "While on a flight from Fort Lauderdale, FL to Dallas/ Forth Worth, the aircraft crashed while making an landing attempt in thunderstorm activity. The plane touched down 6,000 feet short of the runway and 360 feet to the left of the runway centerline, became airborne again, struck a car killing the driver, crossed the highway and crashed into two water tank reservoirs. Microburst induced windshear. The flightcrew's decision to initiate and continue the approach into a cumulonimbus cloud which they observed to contain lightning. Lack of training for avoiding and escaping from low-altitude windshear.";
        schema:location          "Ft. Worth-Dallas" .

