:1968-05-03-lockheed-l188a-electra-id-4547
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Lockheed L188A Electra";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "15:48";
        ex:operator              "Braniff Airlines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "85"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "85"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Texas";
        ex:route                 "Houston - Dallas-Fort Worth";
        dcterms:date             "1968-05-03"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "On a flight from Houston to Dallas the airliner flew into thunderstorms. While attempting to turn around by making a right hand turn, winds lifted the port wing, forcing the starboard wing down past 90 degrees.  A stall resulted from this unusual attitude, pitching the nose down. During the recovery maneuver, the starboard wing was over-stressed, separating from the aircraft followed by the the tail and engines. The aircraft crashed into a field. Pilot's decision to penetrate a line of thunderstorms and severe weather. Visual perception of the pilot may have been reduced by a near lightning strike.";
        schema:location          "Near Dawson" .

