        ex:region                "New Guinea";
        ex:route                 "Lae - Howland Island";
        dcterms:date             "1937-07-02"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The plane disappeared while en route from  Lae to Howland Island. The aircraft had to be flown higher than expected due to storms which used extra fuel.  In addition, strong head winds were encountered.  The aircraft most likely ran out of fuel and ditched into the ocean 50 to 100 miles northwest of Howland Island. Amelia Earhart, 40, and navigator Fred Noonan, killed.";
        schema:location          "Off Lae" .

