        dcterms:description      "The aircraft experienced two missing landing attempts. On the third try, the crew tried to descent below minimum safe altitude to make visual contact with the ground. The right wing clipped trees and the aircraft crashed about 2 m from the runway. Attempting to land in meteorological conditions that were below minima.";
        schema:location          "Near La  Corunda" .

:1993-07-12-cessna-402c-id-3260
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Cessna 402C";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:operator              "Hyannis Air Service - Air Taxi";
        ex:passengersAboard      "3"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "3"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Nevada";
        dcterms:date             "1993-07-12"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The pilot told the local controller that the baggage door was open and he requested a 'go around.' the local controller told the pilot to make right traffic. Multiple witnesses saw the airplane in a nose high attitude during the initial climb after takeoff. They reported the pilot entered a right turn which continued until the airplane 'fell to the ground and hit nose first.  The pilot's failure to maintain adequate airspeed while maneuvering in the traffipattern. A factor which contributed to the accident was the pilot's failure to assure that the nose baggage compartment door was secured.";
        schema:location          "Las Vegas" .

