:1965-12-04-boeing-b-707-131b---l1049c-constellation-id-3383
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Boeing B-707-131B / L1049C Constellation";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "16:18";
        ex:operator              "Trans World Airlines / Eastern Air Lines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "112"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "4"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "New York";
        ex:route                 "Boston - Newark";
        dcterms:date             "1965-12-04"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "Midair collision at 11,000 feet. Misjudgment of altitude separation by the crew of EAL 853 because of an optical illusion created by the up-slope effect of cloud tops resulting in an evasive maneuver by the EAL 853 crew and a reactionary evasive maneuver by  the TWA 42 crew. The 707 landed at JFK despite losing 25 feet of the left wing. There were no injuries to the crew of 7 and 51 passengers aboard the 707.  Three of the 46 passengers and 1 crew member aboard  EAL 853 were killed. Misjudgment of altitude separation by the crew of the Constellation because of an optical illusion created by the up-slope effect of cloud tops, resulting in an evasive maneuver by the Constellation crew and a reactionary evasive maneuver by the Boeing crew.";
        schema:location          "Carmel" .

