:1999-06-01-mcdonnell-douglas-md-82-id-414
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "McDonnell Douglas MD-82";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "23:50";
        ex:operator              "American Airlines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "145"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "11"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Arkansas";
        ex:route                 "Dallas-Fort Worth - Little Rock";
        dcterms:date             "1999-06-01"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "The plane was on a flight from Dallas/Fort Worth, Texas to Little Rock, Arkansas. While attempting to land at Little Rock Airport, the flight encountered heavy thunderstorms, rain and strong winds. The aircraft landed fast and hard, skidded off the end of the runway and struck a landing light tower, breaking into three parts and bursting into flames. Crew's decision to continue the approach despite severe thunderstorms in the area and crosswinds that  exceeded American Airlines' guidelines. The crew did not arm the automatispoiler system before landing or manually deploy the spoilers after touchdown. Fatigue, the crew had been awake for nearly 16 hours.";
        schema:location          "Little Rock" .

:1985-08-25-beechcraft-99-id-2870
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Beechcraft 99";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "22:05";
        ex:operator              "Bar Harbor Airlines";
        ex:passengersAboard      "8"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "8"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Maine";
        ex:route                 "Boston, MA - Auburn, ME";
        dcterms:date             "1985-08-25"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "While on approach, ATC noticed the flight was east of course and the crew was given instructions to correct.   The crew then tried, unsuccessfully to intercept the glideslope. The plane struck trees and crashed short and right of the runway centerline. The pilot's continuation of an unstabilized approach which resulted in a descent below glideslope. Improper IFR procedure by pilot. Missed approach not performed. Decision height not identified. Samantha Smith, 13, along with her father were killed. She became famous for writing to Soviet leader Yuri Andropov about her fear of nuclear war. She later visited him in Moscow.";
        schema:location          "Auburn" .

