:1961-11-08-lockheed-c-69-constellation-id-4882
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Lockheed C-69 Constellation";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "21:24";
        ex:operator              "Imperial Airways";
        ex:passengersAboard      "79"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "77"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Virginia";
        ex:route                 "Baltimore - Columbia SC";
        dcterms:date             "1961-11-08"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "Flown under a military contract, several procedural errors by the crew caused the loss of 2 engines. After several more errors, the aircraft crashed into a wooded area. Most deaths from post-impact fire and CO.  Lack of command coordination and decision, faulty judgement and insufficient knowledge that led to an emergency situation. In addition there were faulty maintenance procedures. The carrier's license was revoked 6 weeks after the crash.";
        schema:location          "Near Richmond" .

:1966-09-22-vickers-viscount-832-id-498
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Vickers Viscount 832";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "13:03";
        ex:operator              "Ansett ANA";
        ex:passengersAboard      "24"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "24"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Australia";
        ex:route                 "Mount Isa - Longreach";
        dcterms:date             "1966-09-22"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "About 150 miles from Longreach, fire was reported in No. 1 and 2 engines. While the plane was making an emergency descent, the left wing broke away due to weakening by the fire. After failure of the wing, the plane broke up in mid-air and crashed. Loosened bolts led to the loss of the oil lubricating unit causing the bearings to heat and catching the engines on fire. Subsequently, a locking mechanism was installed on the bolts to prevent any future accidents of this kind.";
        schema:location          "Winton" .

<http://example.org/crash/1918-04-07-zeppelin-l-59-(airship)-id-5199>
