        dcterms:description      "The plane crashed and burned 6.5 miles west northwest of the Bubank Airport in dense fog. The pilot's deviation from the standard instrument approach procedure and descent below the established safe minimum altitude. A contributing factor was the company's failure to enforce adherence to company procedures.";
        schema:location          "Van Nuys" .

:1947-01-25-douglas-c-47---douglas-dc-3-id-1654
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Douglas C-47 / Douglas DC-3";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:operator              "Spencer Airways / Ceskoslovenske Aerolinie";
        ex:passengersAboard      "23"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "12"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "England";
        ex:route                 "Guangzhou - Chongqing";
        dcterms:date             "1947-01-25"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "Just after becoming airborne, the plane never gained altitude, overran the runway and crashed into a Ceskoslovenske Dakota. Twelve killed on the Spencer Airways none on the Ceskoslovenske. Loss of control by the captain of the Spencer Airways plane, who, when attempting to take-off a heavily loaded aircraft in poor visibility allowed it to become airborne in a semi-stalled condition.";
        schema:location          "Surrey" .

:2005-02-16-cessna-560-citation-v-id-1432
        rdf:type                 schema:Event;
        ex:aircraftType          "Cessna 560 Citation V";
        ex:groundFatalities      "0"^^xsd:int;
        ex:hour                  "09:13";
        ex:operator              "Circuit City Stores - Charter";
        ex:passengersAboard      "8"^^xsd:int;
        ex:passengersFatalities  "8"^^xsd:int;
        ex:region                "Colorado";
        ex:route                 "Richmond, VA - Saint Louis, MO  - Pueblo,CO - Irvine, CA";
        dcterms:date             "2005-02-16"^^xsd:date;
        dcterms:description      "While on approach the business flight descended through IMC until the left wing contacted the ground. The plane crashed into a field and burned. The plane crashed because the pilots failed to notice the airplane had slowed to an unsafe speed and allowed the plane to stall. In addition, there was a thin layer of ice on the aircraft's wings. The flight crew's failure to effectively monitor and maintain airspeed and comply with procedures for deice boot activation on the approach, which caused an aerodynamistall from which they did not recover. Contributing to the accident was the FAA's failure to establish adequate certification requirements for flight into icing conditions, which led to the inadequate stall warning margin provided by the airplane's stall warning system.";
        schema:location          "Near Pueblo" .

